O3DE: SSAO's sampling radius and blur
=====================================

SSAO's sampling radius swept, with and without its blur, measured against SSAO off, with the GPU time of each pass
(lab/src/experiment.rs has the format; the lab reads the binding `ssao` as that TOML document, lab/src/script/data.rs).
Run it with:

    render-lab --investigation o3de/lighting experiment o3de_lighting.experiment/ssao --out <dir>

$[Import* std]

The radii swept, in metres.
$[# _radii [% {' 0.02 0.05 0.1 0.2}]]

$[# ssao {.
    name "ssao"
    description "O3DE's SSAO sampling radius swept, with and without its blur, against no SSAO."
    investigation "o3de/lighting"
    demo "ssao"
    resolution {' 1280 720}
    frames 2
    warmup 30
    repeats 30
    metrics {' "gpu_ms" "mse" "psnr" "ssim" "flip" "luminance"}
    base {. values {. viewMode "final"}}
    reference {. values {. ssao false}}
    sweep {' {. values {. ssaoRadius _radii}}}
    variant {' {. name "no-blur" values {. ssaoBlur false}}}}]
